				<p class="home-statement"><strong>Terminus Foundry</strong> provides AI &amp; security services, helping engineering businesses make AI, data &amp; software work, safely.</p>
				<img eleventy:ignore class="home-photo home-photo-wide" src="/images/home/devon-boulton-mills.jpg" alt="Portrait of Devon Boulton-Mills" width="480" height="480">
				<p class="home-statement">I'm <strong>Devon Boulton-Mills</strong>, a senior technology leader and engineer operating out of the UK. For more than 15 years I have built businesses, led technical teams and delivered enterprise software for clients around the world, with a focus on security. I like solving real problems with people, software &amp; hardware.</p>
			</section>

			<section id="work">
				<p class="home-statement">Today I am co-founder &amp; COO of <strong>Decimo</strong>, an engineering-intelligence company in electric propulsion, where I run operations, AI, data &amp; software. Before that, most of my work sat where engineering meets data &amp; software. I led technical programmes for <strong>Arrival</strong>'s 60-engineer electric-vehicle simulation group, across four vehicle platforms. I ran operations on the executive team at <strong>Seabird Technologies</strong>, in electric boat racing &amp; electric powertrain development. I led data &amp; operations work at <strong>Shell</strong> and <strong>Air Canada</strong>, and co-founded an enterprise software company that grew revenue 600%. I am a professional electrical engineer.</p>
				{# Where Devon has worked, as a fact of employment, not clients or endorsements: each company's own mark, linked to its website.
				   Arrival is gone (administration, 2024), so it links to its Wikipedia article. Sources: README.md, "Company logos". #}
				<ul class="home-logos" aria-label="Where I have worked">
					<li><a href="https://www.decimo.tech/"><img eleventy:ignore class="logo-decimo" src="/assets/logos/companies/decimo-mark.png" alt="Decimo website" width="178" height="257"></a></li>
					<li><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrival_(company)"><img eleventy:ignore class="logo-arrival" src="/assets/logos/companies/arrival-mark.svg" alt="Arrival on Wikipedia" width="210" height="208"></a></li>
					<li><a href="https://seabird.tech/"><img eleventy:ignore class="logo-seabird" src="/assets/logos/companies/seabird-mark.png" alt="Seabird Technologies website" width="217" height="114"></a></li>
					<li><a href="https://www.shell.com/"><img eleventy:ignore class="logo-shell" src="/assets/logos/companies/shell.svg" alt="Shell website" width="150" height="139"></a></li>
					<li><a href="https://www.aircanada.com/"><img eleventy:ignore class="logo-air-canada" src="/assets/logos/companies/air-canada-mark.svg" alt="Air Canada website" width="129" height="127"></a></li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section id="services">
				<p class="home-statement">What I help with:</p>
				<ul class="home-list">
					<li><strong>Secure AI adoption.</strong> A practical plan to roll AI tools and agents out across a company, with the right controls on identity, data &amp; access, so people use them and trust them.</li>
					<li><strong>Data foundations.</strong> Data strategy, architecture &amp; quality, from enterprise data warehouses to engineering &amp; field data.</li>
					<li><strong>Software &amp; product.</strong> Building and scaling software products, from founding a company to selling to Fortune 500 clients.</li>
					<li><strong>Operating leadership.</strong> Scaling technical teams, delivery, supply chain &amp; governance in hardware &amp; software businesses.</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section id="guides">
				<p class="home-statement">I care about how technology can best benefit society, and about the move to sustainable energy.</p>
				<p class="home-statement">Back in 2021 I wrote two free guides on those themes; they're a bit out of date, but the core philosophies still stand:</p>
